WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:12,140
Should I continue to do thermography?

00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,180
So I don't know who was asked this question, but yes,

00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,980
if you are doing if you've done the thermography for breast exam,

00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:28,460
I was assuming this person has done thermography for breast exams in the past.

00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:35,580
Maybe got a positive fighting and then maybe went the medical route, had it go again a biopsy, blah, blah, blah.

00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,940
Now they're under care for cancer for breast cancer.

00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,500
Should you continue to do thermography?

00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:47,420
I think highly advisable to continue to do thermography because it can be a very simple,

00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:50,700
not invasive screening tool moving forward.

00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:59,620
Now there may be some some artifacts left over from, let's say the biopsy.

00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:03,460
So you had this in the incision and blah, blah, blah.

00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:06,780
You take that into account when you read the thermography.

00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:11,020
But yes, continue to do thermography.

00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:15,700
It's a great screening tool to screen progress as well.

00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,380
So answer yes.

